        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Tlingit</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">Lingít Aaní, the Land of the Tlingit: from Yakutat south through the Alaskan Panhandle and the Alexander Archipelago, and inland along the Alsek, Tatshenshini, Chilkat, Taku and Stikine rivers to Atlin, Teslin and Tagish Lakes in northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a> and the southern Yukon</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Human culture with elements related to the Tlingit from around 10,000 years ago; first contact with Russian explorers in 1741 and Spanish in 1775; the 1862 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> epidemic; conversions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Christianity</a> between 1886 and 1895; today federally recognised tribes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-nations-in-canada">First Nations in Canada</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">matrilineal clans within the Raven and Eagle moieties; heraldic crests on totem poles, canoes and house posts; cedar plank clan houses; at.oow, inherited objects held in trust; a rich oratory tradition; Chilkat and Ravenstail weaving; salmon fisheries</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Tlingit's own traditions and present-day communities; Russian sources such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigory-shelikhov">Grigory Shelikhov</a>'s 1796 map; ethnographies such as those by Frederica de Laguna, George Thornton Emmons and Sergei Kan; Swanton's Tlingit Myths and Texts (1909); genetic studies of HLA genes</span></div>
