    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Tlingit society is divided into two moieties, the Raven and the Eagle, made up of clans in which descent and inheritance pass through the mother's line.</li><li>The 1862 Pacific Northwest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> epidemic killed about 60% of the Mainland Tlingit and 37% of the Island Tlingit.</li><li>Tribes, institutions and linguists are working to revitalise the Tlingit language, which has an estimated 200 to 400 speakers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and 100 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The name Lingít means 'People of the Tides', while the old Russian name for them, Koloshi, came from a Sugpiaq-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alutiiq">Alutiiq</a> word for the labret worn by women.</p></aside>
    </section>

